      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks unsafe, and I'd like you to confirm it first.\n\n**The problem:** Metformin 1700 mg three times daily adds up to **5100 mg/day**. The usual maximum for adults is **2550 mg/day** for immediate-release and **2000 mg/day** for extended-release. This order is twice the maximum, which raises the risk of severe GI side effects and lactic acidosis.\n\n**What you may have meant:**\n- **850 mg by mouth, three times daily with meals.** That's 2550 mg/day, the maximum immediate-release dose. 850 mg is a standard tablet strength, so 1700 might be a doubled 850.\n- **1700 mg/day total**, split into doses (for example, 850 mg twice daily with meals).\n- **Another dose or schedule.** If so, please give me the details.\n\nAlso, please confirm whether this should be **immediate-release or extended-release**, since they have different maximums and dosing schedules.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose and schedule, I'll enter the order right away. If 1700 mg three times daily really is intended, I'll need a reason I can add as a note on the order."
      }
