       "text": "I can't enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. The total dose, 5100 mg/day, is twice the maximum, and I don't know of any recognized clinical reason for a metformin dose that high. You didn't give a reason, so there's nothing to show this is anything other than a likely error. The risks to the patient (lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity) are serious enough that I shouldn't be the one to submit it.\n\nHere are some options:\n\n1. **I can enter 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals right now.** That's 2550 mg/day, the maximum dose.\n2. **I can enter a different dose or schedule** within the usual range.\n3. **If this dose really is intended** (for example, as part of a protocol or under specialist direction), please discuss it with the clinical pharmacist or attending and enter the order through the system's usual override process, recording the reason. That way it gets the independent safety check a dose this far above the maximum needs.\n\nLet me know if you'd like option 1 or 2, and I'll enter it right away."
